OL,3,GUK long range forecast
OL,4,
OL,5,COutlook for Sun 23 Aug to Tue 1 Sep
OL,6,FThis period is likely to start largely
OL,7,Fdry and settled across the UK, as a
OL,8,Fridge of high pressure sets in. A few
OL,9,Fshowers are likely in the far north
OL,10,Fand possibly the far southeast though.
OL,11,FConditions look like turning
OL,12,Fincreasingly unsettled through next
OL,13,Fweek, as low pressure gradually
OL,14,Fbecomes dominant, squeezing the ridge
OL,15,Foff to the northeast. Most places are
OL,16,Flikely to see some rain or showers,
OL,17,Fparticularly during the second half of
OL,18,Fnext week, and these may be heavy with
OL,19,Fa risk of hail and thunder. It may
OL,20,Fbecome breezy if not windy at times
OL,21,Ftoo. Temperatures are likely to be
OL,22,Fnear or a little below normal overall,
OL,23,QppppppppppppppppppppGSource: Met Office
OL,23,Fwith some chilly nights at first, but
OL,24,ANext Page  BWeather  CReg News  FReg TV
OL,24,Fbrief warm, humid spells are possible
OL,25,Fat times, especially in the south.
